From: seilent <github@seilent.net>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:19:27 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] driver core: leave the link status alone when the supplier
 check defers

device_links_check_suppliers() sets links.status to DL_DEV_PROBING also
when it returns -EPROBE_DEFER. really_probe() then returns without
calling device_links_no_driver(), so a device that waits for a supplier
keeps reading DL_DEV_PROBING while it sits on the deferred probe list.

A managed link added to such a device starts in DL_STATE_CONSUMER_PROBE
instead of DL_STATE_DORMANT. The bind of the new supplier then skips the
link and never queues the consumer for probe, and an unbind of the
supplier loops in device_links_unbind_consumers() waiting for a probe
that is not running.

Set DL_DEV_PROBING only when the device goes on to probe, on 0 and on the
best effort -EAGAIN, and leave the status as it was on -EPROBE_DEFER.
---
 drivers/base/core.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/base/core.c b/drivers/base/core.c
index 4d0266829..3f77f22a3 100644
--- a/drivers/base/core.c
+++ b/drivers/base/core.c
@@ -1164,7 +1164,8 @@ int device_links_check_suppliers(struct device *dev)
 		}
 		WRITE_ONCE(link->status, DL_STATE_CONSUMER_PROBE);
 	}
-	dev->links.status = DL_DEV_PROBING;
+	if (ret != -EPROBE_DEFER)
+		dev->links.status = DL_DEV_PROBING;
 
 	device_links_write_unlock();
 
